!SSHd - an SSH server for RISC OS 5
====================================

Double-click !SSHd to start the server in a TaskWindow.  It listens on
TCP port 22 and accepts public-key logins only.

Setup
-----
Configuration lives in <Choices$Write>.SSHd (normally !Boot.Choices.SSHd):

  authkeys   Your SSH public keys, one per line, in the format ssh-keygen
             writes to id_ed25519.pub / id_rsa.pub (OpenSSH authorized_keys
             format, options prefixes are not supported).  The file is
             created empty on first run; nobody can log in until you fill it.
  hostkey    The server's ed25519 host key, generated on first run using the
             CryptRandom module.  Delete it to generate a new one.

Use
---
  ssh user@riscos-host '*Cat'      run one command, output comes back
  ssh user@riscos-host             line-mode * prompt; 'exit' or Ctrl-D ends

The user name is not checked; only the key is.  Commands run through OS_CLI
inside the server's own task with their VDU output captured to a file, so
they cannot be interactive and must not start a Wimp application.  A
TaskWindow-based interactive session is planned.

Options (edit !Run or run sshd from a TaskWindow by hand):
  -p port    listen on another port
  -d dir     use another configuration directory
  -v         verbose logging (-vv includes SSH protocol messages)
